{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Moses stretched out</b> his hand — One needs to examine a fine point: why in the plague of locusts, which is adjacent to it, even though HaShem said to him, ״Stretch out your hand,״ the verse says ״And Moses stretched out his staff״ and so forth (Exodus 10:13), and also in all the plagues there was no plague in which the stretching out of a hand was mentioned — only a staff; but in this plague it says <b>his hand.</b>" "Or perhaps it intends according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 14:2), that the darkness of Egypt was from that very darkness of which it is written (Psalms 18:12): ״יָשֶׁת חֹשֶׁךְ סִתְרוֹ״ — therefore he did not conduct himself in the manner of diminishing honor by stretching his staff upward." "<b>Also,</b> there are some of our Rabbis who said (Exodus Rabbah 14:2) that this darkness was from Gehenna. Perhaps both of them intended the truth, for there were two kinds of darkness: one that functioned during the three days when they did not see, and so forth, and one that functioned during three other days when they did not rise, and so forth."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:25.268059349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}